(type apse_exec_t)
(roletype object_r apse_exec_t)
(type apse_t)
(roletype object_r apse_t)
(roletype unconfined_r apse_t)
(type apse_app_t)
(roletype object_r apse_app_t)
(roletype unconfined_r apse_app_t)
; decision #42: the pdeathsig-restore shim (.so) type. A confined
; consumer must *map it with PROT_EXEC* — on this kernel a PROT_EXEC
; mapping needs `file:execute` (file_map_prot_to_av), which no
; base-policy type grants to `apse_app_t`/`xserver_t` on a file in
; the instance runtime dir. Dedicated type, NOT a member of `lib_t`
; (which every app type can read): the two consumer types below get
; the grants, nothing else can touch it. `ensure_shim` relabels the
; compiled `.so` to it with setxattr (on this kernel `filecon`
; statements do not label created inodes and their contexts are not
; pre-registered in the sidtab — the sidtab expands on demand).
(type apse_shim_t)
(roletype object_r apse_shim_t)
; decision #43 (refined): the per-app state tree
; (`$XDG_STATE_HOME/apse/` — on Fedora `~/.local/state/apse/`) gets
; a dedicated type instead of riding `gconf_home_t`. That label
; only reached the tree by accident: the gnome module's filecon
; `HOME_DIR/\.local(/.*)?` is broad enough to label *all* of
; `~/.local` (everything but `.local/share`) with it. A module
; type joins no base attribute by default (LESSONS #53) — in
; particular it is *not* a member of `user_home_type`, so no
; base-policy or other-module grant ever reaches the tree: only
; this module's explicit grants apply (the apse domains, plus the
; user's unconfined lifecycle). Labeling (verified against the
; 7.2 source, `security/selinux/hooks.c` + `ss/services.c`): a
; created inode takes the filetrans result for (creator, parent,
; class) — `filecon` does not label created inodes on this
; kernel (`selinux_determine_inode_label` consults only an
; mntpoint default, a process `create_sid`, or filetrans) — so
; the named filetrans below makes the `apse` root
; `apse_state_t` and everything beneath it inherits the label
; (the no-rule default of `security_compute_sid` is the parent's
; own type: one rule labels the whole tree, any depth, any fs).
; The range takes the parent's low level (MLS target-low: `s0`,
; dominated by every `s0:cN`). S's runtime `setxattr` walk
; (`prepare_app_state` — the same mechanism as `apse_shim_t`)
; performs the one-time migration of a pre-module (gconf-labelled)
; tree and self-heals any straggler: on this kernel the relabel
; path checks ownership, `relabelfrom` (subject → the inode's old
; label), `relabelto` (subject → this one), the class
; `validatetrans` constraint, and `associate` (this SID → the
; mount's SID), and the pre-check label read (`getxattr
; "security.selinux"`) carries no MAC check
; (`selinux_inode_getsecurity` only converts the inode's SID).
(type apse_state_t)
(roletype object_r apse_state_t)
